  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a red car overturned on the side of a road, with the text overlay stating, 'this is what happens when you don't spank your kids.' This meme uses a visual of a car accident to make a causal and punitive argument about child-rearing. The intent is to suggest that physical punishment (spanking) is a necessary or protective measure to prevent negative outcomes, implying that its absence leads to dangerous consequences. This is a harmful meme because it promotes corporal punishment as a solution to behavioral problems, which is widely discredited by child development experts and public health organizations for its potential to cause physical and psychological harm to children. It also normalizes violence as a parenting tool, which can contribute to a culture of abuse and may influence parents to use physical discipline. The meme's overall intent is to instill fear and guilt in parents who do not use spanking, thereby promoting a specific, harmful parenting ideology.",
